# Keep the Docker build context small and correct.
#
# This file's absence caused the first publish-image failure: the Dockerfile's
# builder stage does `COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules` and then `COPY . .`,
# so a node_modules present on the host was copied straight over the one
# installed inside the image. That host copy carries pnpm metadata pointing at
# a different store, so pnpm's deps-status check decided it had to purge
# node_modules and aborted with ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY
# (a Docker build has no TTY to confirm at).
#
# It also keeps ~1 GB out of the context, which is most of the build time.

# Dependencies and build output — always provided inside the image
node_modules
.next
out

# Never put secrets in a build context
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
test.env

# Not needed to build
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
tests
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
*.log
*.report.html
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
